### Render only available response times (4/5)

**Severity:** `medium`

When the model has no valid response-time sample, the card should omit that field instead of passing an invalid value to the formatter. This keeps the displayed measurement consistent with the nullable model.

```suggestion
            if (diskStats.ResponseTime is float responseTime)
            {
                ContentData["diskResponseTime"] = ResponseTimeToString(responseTime);
            }

```

### Cover non-finite response-time readings (5/5)

**Severity:** `medium`

Cover NaN and both infinities as unavailable, while retaining the finite negative-value clamp and a positive sample. These cases protect the policy without depending on hardware-generated counter readings.

```suggestion
{
    [TestMethod]
    public void ResponseTimeIsUnavailableWhenTheReadingIsNotFinite()
    {
        Assert.IsNull(DiskStats.GetResponseTime(float.NaN));
        Assert.IsNull(DiskStats.GetResponseTime(float.PositiveInfinity));
        Assert.IsNull(DiskStats.GetResponseTime(float.NegativeInfinity));
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void ResponseTimeClampsFiniteNegativeReadingsToZero()
    {
        Assert.AreEqual(0f, DiskStats.GetResponseTime(-0.001f).Value);
        Assert.AreEqual(0.001f, DiskStats.GetResponseTime(0.001f).Value);
    }

```
